==Appearance==
<tabber>
|-|Default=
Waxwell appears to be a purple candle with tons of wax dripping off, acting as his hair. The top of his head has a white wick which has a large, orange flame on top when his [[Ability]] is active, making him glow brighter in [[Blackouts]]. He wears a white-spiked, red collar around his neck, a short, dark gray, bell-sleeved cloth with a jagged hem, and red boots. He also appears to have eye bags under his eyes.

|-|Vintage=
Vintage Waxwell is gray with his eyes pie-cut to the left and has a black wick that produces a white flame. His collar spikes and cloth are black, and his collar and boots are white.

|-|Villainous Casual=
Villainous Casual Waxwell has the wax become a medium warm gray instead of purple, and gives him a bright red headband with two horns. He now wears a bright red sweater, with black sleeve cuffs, alongside some red and white sneakers. His spiked collar now has a black base instead of a red one, and he dons two black loops on each of his thighs. He gains a light gray pair of pants, with ripped knees, and has one black triangle under each eye. His wick now generates a red flame.

|-|Toxic Experiment=
Toxic Experiment Waxwell's wax is a notably warmer shade of purple than before, and his eye bags have become a bright magenta, alongside his boots. He has more wax on his head, acting as fluffy bangs, alongside a set of black goggles, with green lenses inside. These lenses have a mint green to lime green gradient. Instead of a spiked collar, he now wears a pastel green turtle-neck sweater and some pitch black pants. He wears a white lab coat as well, which is visibly worn and stained with pale red. His flame is now a bright green instead of orange.
</tabber>

==Personality==
Waxwell is a mischievous [[Toon]], though unlike {{CI|Gigi|name=true}}, he takes slightly more drastic measures, doing pranks with seemingly more malicious intent like stealing {{CI|Toodles|name=true}}' {{TI|Dog Plush|name=true}} and attempting to burn it. He has also added extra things to {{CI|Sprout|name=true}} and {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}}'s baked goods with the intent of ruining the recipes, only for Sprout to thank him for supposedly helping them in their interaction. Apparently, these pranks always backfire, either by him messing up or other Toons accepting it, sometimes even reacting positively. When things don't go as planned, he throws a tantrum, trying to either downplay his failures or twist the situation to make it seen like his antics worked, as seen in multiple interactions. Waxwell also tries to ignore things to make his claims work sometimes, like when he denied research about dinosaurs in dialogue with {{CI|Shelly|name=true}}. He also makes attempts to immolate other Toons and their stuff, like how he jokingly considered burning {{CI|Flutter|name=true}}'s wings, only for her to immediately berate him for that. 

It seems like he has a softer side or at least is not as malicious or "evil" as he tries to act. When {{CI|Goob|name=true}} offers to hug him, he considers it, but immediately backtracks and threatens Goob. He is also self conscious of the fact his plans always backfire and how he never seemed to succeed in the [[Show]], as is evident while talking with {{CI|Glisten|name=true}} and {{CI|Vee|name=true}}. This is likely the reason of his almost-constant tiredness, only being relieved of it when attempting a [[Abilities|''prank'']], but continuing to fail repeatedly, despite {{CI|Dandy|name=true}}'s belief that Waxwell is not impacted by the constant failure of his pranks. Suggested by his {{CI|Twisted Waxwell}}[[Twisted Waxwell|Twisted counterpart]]'s scrawny, seemingly starved appearance, he may have burned so much energy into trying to conduct a successful prank, that he deprived his body of sufficient support to a greater extent than visible in his Toon form.

