==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first requirement, you need to walk into {{CI|Twisted Waxwell|name=true}} to obtain [[Research]]. Playing as {{CI|Rodger|name=true}} also helps getting it faster because of his Passive [[Ability]]. This will be easier if Twisted Waxwell is on the [[Daily Twisted Board]].
*For the second requirement, play as {{CI|Goob|name=true}} and try to complete 3 of his [[Mastery]] Quests by going on multiple runs. Since you only need to complete half of the total mastery quests to buy Waxwell, choose some specific missions, preferably the easiest ones.
*For the third requirement, focus on picking up [[Research Capsules]] and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Capsule count increases the further you descend, so you can earn more {{II|Ichor|name=true}}.
==Strategies==
Waxwell, if used properly, is a really versatile [[Toon]], being a great distractor, decent extractor, and adequate support.

Waxwell's 5{{Star}} [[Movement Speed]] and 2 Star [[Stealth]] makes him an almost perfect Distractor, not having the problems other great distractors have, like {{CI|Pebble|name=true}}'s 3 Star Stealth or {{CI|Looey|name=true}}'s need to get hit to be faster. However, he has a major drawback: his Stamina. On top of 1 Star Stamina, his (almost) constant {{Debuff|Tired|II}} makes Stamina an extremely limited resource. Although this could be fine with good Stamina management, hard [[Twisted]] combinations will be a lot harder, as things like sprint-tapping, maneuvering, or rounding up Twisteds will use up a large chunk of Waxwell's Stamina. Additionally, during [[Panic Mode]], reaching the [[Elevator]] will be difficult, especially if really far away, risking death, even with your 5 Star Movement. However, you could have Toons like {{CI|Astro|name=true}} or {{CI|Tisha|name=true}} help with mobility, either reducing the need for Stamina or numbing the consequences of using it. You can also use mobility or Stamina [[Trinkets]] like {{TI|Dog Plush|name=true}} or {{TI|Cooler|name=true}} to ease the weakness. It can be really beneficial to select both {{CDI|Well-Paced/Endurance|name=true}} Cards, as his capacity will be increased to 120. Additionally, his [[Ability]], {{AI|Waxwell|name=true}}, can help these Toons use their Abilities more often, letting them help other Toons more efficiently or help you more often. This also removes his Tired II, so you reap more benefits, getting support and more reliable Stamina regeneration. His 2 Star Stealth also lets him solar-kite with {{CI|Bobette|name=true}} (albeit a Stealth-affecting Trinket is needed), somewhat fixing his Stamina problem and letting him move quick, but certain combos can still be quite dangerous and difficult to handle.

If you want to use Waxwell for extracting, his 5 Star Skill Check still makes him really good with [[Machines]], though his Extraction Speed is quite low. Because of this, he relies on his Skill Checks to let him progress through the Machines, so Trinkets like {{TI|Magnifying Glass|name=true}} or {{TI|Participation Award|name=true}} can help him finish faster. He could also use his Ability to reduce the cooldowns of Toons like {{CI|Shelly|name=true}} or {{CI|Squirm|name=true}}'s Abilities, letting them use their Abilities more and quickening Machine completion. On top of that, his high Movement Speed makes Treadmill Machines also quickly done, albeit the low Stamina makes sprinting on them less common, making it slightly slow. Barnaby Machines are also less of a risk with his high Skill Check, and the coins give a high value, making his low Extraction Speed less of an issue. However, do note the 2 Star Stealth is an issue if you aren't distracting, and certain Machines could be out of reach due to distractors.

Finally, his Ability makes supporting others really easy, with the only downside being his 60 second cooldown and the need to move around. If a player were to stand in the flame trail for the minimum 10 seconds (+5 seconds of lingering), they would have approximately 30 seconds cut from their cooldown, though they could cut even more time if they follow the entire trail, as each flame lasts for 10 seconds (for an overall duration of around 20 seconds, from the first flame spawning, to the last few flames disappearing), meaning a player could theoretically cut down nearly 50 seconds. This maximized cooldown reduction is of course really situational, being reliant on the Waxwell moving for the entirety that his Ability is active, and only really useful on select Toons (e.g. a Toon with a healing Ability, who needs to heal a teammate or multiple, but is held back by their cooldown), as otherwise this could take up time away from extracting from fast extractors. 

With his Ability activated, he also glows in [[Blackouts]] (albeit really little) and loses the Tired II, letting him move around more quickly and spread his trail. When his Ability is active, you should try running around as much as possible, covering as much area as possible so Toons know where the trail is. You can also put it in a small space and tell Toons where it is so they can simply stay still or move around in the trail. This can especially be done while distracting, though high Stealth Toons will be the only ones able to get to him without endangering the rest. Since he loses his Tired II while his Ability is active, you could use it after being chased to recover Stamina a bit faster, though this should usually only be done if nobody is in need of the cooldown reduction, or won't be affected by it. You could also use it during Panic Mode or a particularly dangerous moment when you absolutely need to recover a bit more Stamina than you otherwise would with the Tired II.

He can be great on [[Dyle's Floor]] due to his versatility. His maximum Skill Check means failing is less likely, which can make {{CI|Twisted Dyle|name=true}} less of a threat, and even if someone fails a Skill Check, Waxwell has the speed to make a quick getaway. He can take care of Treadmill Machines rather efficiently and can use his Ability on certain Toons to get through Machines faster. Plus, the extra +50 Stamina capacity given for completing the Floor can improve his survivability, especially when combined with both Well-Paced/Endurance Cards, since he'll have a capacity of 170, nearly 4 Stars.

In solo runs, his strengths become a lot more apparent. His 5 Star Movement Speed lets him escape almost all of the Twisteds, though without anyone distracting, regenerating and managing Stamina will be harder. His high Skill Check makes doing Machines easier too, also lessening the amount of Skill Check failures and Twisted attractions, albeit the low Extraction Speed makes you stay on them for a while longer. Despite his Ability's main purpose of decreasing others' cooldowns being useless in a solo scenario, the temporary removal of the Tired II Debuff as well as the light produced from the flames can still provide great benefits.

Overall, despite his shortcomings, he is able to adequately do everything so long as you play right. He's really capable of many tasks, but is reliant on good skill and knowledge of the game as well as experience with distracting if you decide to do so with him. He's a very good choice for solo runs due to his high speed and above average extraction, though you'll have to keep an eye on his shortcomings.

