==Trivia==
*Waxwell's name could be a portmanteau of the word "Wax" and the name "Maxwell".
*Waxwell is the first [[Toon]] to have a name starting with and containing the letter W.
*Waxwell is the second non-[[Main]] [[Toon]] to have permanent 5{{Star}} in two [[Stats]], with the first being {{CI|Soulvester|name=true}}.
**Additionally, he is the first non-Main '''and''' non-[[Event]] Toon to have this trait.
**Coincidentally, he shares 5 Stars in Skill Check and 1 Star in Stamina with Soulvester.
*Waxwell is the first [[Toon]] with 5 Stars in [[Movement Speed]] to:
**Not be a {{Type|Main}}.
***Though you can argue that {{CI|Razzle & Dazzle|name=true}} and {{CI|Looey|name=true}} can have 5 Stars in Movement Speed, Razzle & Dazzle only get 5 Star Speed on odd Floors and Looey needs to be at 1 Heart to achieve an approximation of 5 Star Speed. Waxwell has it exactly and consistently.
****You could also argue that Looey's speed is also consistent, but once he gets healed, he loses speed.
**Not have 4 Stars in [[Stamina]].
**Have above average Skill Check.
**Not have an [[Ability]] related to [[Items]], nor a Passive Ability.
**Not have a [[Gamepass]] [[Skin]].
**Not have a [[Mastery]] Quest requiring reaching [[Floor]] 20.
*Waxwell, alongside {{CI|Glisten|name=true}}, is one of the few [[Toons]] who applies a [[Status Effect]] to themself.
**Waxwell is the first to have a Debuff constantly applied to himself.
**Waxwell is also the first one to inflict Buffs (positive Status Effects) to other Toons.
*Waxwell and {{CI|Squirm|name=true}} have some similarities.
**They have new letters no other [[Toons]] have in their name.
**They both frequently show negative emotions, with Waxwell being "malice" and Squirm being distressed.
**They have 5 Stars on an Extracting [[Stat]].
**Their Twisteds are {{Type|Rares}}.
**Both require 50% [[Research]] of their [[Twisted]] counterparts to obtain.
**They both have 2 Stars in [[Stealth]].
**They were the only Toons released in 2026.
***Although 2026 hasn't ended yet, with the coming months being unlikely to release a full-fledged Toon, they are most likely to be the only ones releasing.
**They have the ability to speed up an [[Ability]]'s cooldown by 2 times.
***These affects stack too; Having Squirm affected by {{Debuff|Ignited}} while eating books reduces his cooldown 4 times faster.<ref>[[File:x4 Ability Cooldown.gif]]</ref>
**They had prior teasers that showed a vague sense of what they were (Squirm's silhouette and Waxwell's candlewick), before getting a short that fully revealed them a few days before their releases.
*Waxwell is the first [[Toon]] to need the use of a [[Trinket]] to complete a [[Mastery]] quest. He is additionally the first Toon to require extracting a specific [[Machine]] type, and the second to require using a specific [[Item]].
*Waxwell is so far the longest [[Toon]] to be in development before their release, taking 662 days. Before, many ideas for his character were teased around by [[Qwel]].
**The idea for his personality was shared on October 15, 2024.<ref>https://discordapp.com/channels/969934252844138496/1251545388259741768/1296100038203805698</ref>
**The idea for his gimmick<ref>https://discordapp.com/channels/969934252844138496/1251545388259741768/1385976852790906940</ref>(his {{Debuff|Tired|II}} Debuff) and Movement Speed [[Stat]] wasn't shared till June 20, 2024.
**His early concept art was created around March/April 2026.<ref>https://x.com/Aaron_Margolin/status/2083996147098816889?s=20</ref>
*Waxwell is the third [[Toon]] whose [[Introduction Card]] did not come with him upon his release, with the first being {{CI|Yatta|name=true}} and the second being {{CI|Brusha|name=true}}.
**Additionally, he's the first male Toon to not have an Introduction Card come upon his release.
*Waxwell, along with [[Yatta]], [[Brusha]], {{CI|Blot|name=true}}, {{CI|Finn|name=true}}, and {{CI|Gigi|name=true}} are one of the only [[Toons]] to not have a full icon.
*Waxwell is the first [[Toon]] to have multiple light radii in [[Blackouts]], with [[Ability]]-activation changing his glow from the default white to a larger red (or other colors depending on [[Skin]]).
**He is the first Toon to not have a light bulb icon signifying the Light-Producing Aux. [[Statistics#Auxiliary Statistics|Stat]], but still glow in Blackouts.
***He shares this trait with {{CI|Ribecca|name=true}} (though for her, it's [[Ichor Puddle]] Immunity), as she also doesn't have a signifying icon either, but still effectively has the associated Aux. Stat.
**He is the only one with a temporary and activatable radius, as all other Light-Producing Toons are permanently and passively glowing in Blackouts.
*Waxwell is the first [[Toon]] to have a trail [[Ability]].
**This also means that he is currently the only Toon to be affected by his [[Trinket]], {{TI|Cherished Blanket|name=true}}.
*Like other recent [[Toons]], Waxwell does not have interactions with nearly half of the Toons despite not being [[Event]]-exclusive, just like [[Blot]] and [[Brusha]].
**Considering that the two mentioned above have had more dialogue added over time, it's possible that Waxwell will also have some, probably in his [[Toon of the Week]].
*Waxwell and {{CI|Bobette|name=true}} have multiple similarities.
**They have unique [[Ability]] types and can have them affected by their respective [[Trinkets]] ([[Cherished Blanket]] and {{TI|Toy Kit|name=true}}).
***They are also the only ones with those Ability types and therefore the only one able to use said Trinkets.
**They have 5 Stars in a mobility [[Stat]], 2 Stars in [[Extraction Speed]], and 2 Stars in [[Stealth]].
***In fact, prior to Bobette's stat change, they both had 5 Stars in Skill Check as well.
**They have Abilities that affect Stamina in a way.
*Waxwell technically needs 2 different [[Toons]] to be unlocked, as you can only purchase {{CI|Goob|name=true}} if you have 3 quests on {{CI|Scraps|name=true}}'s [[Mastery]] done.
**This makes him the third Toon to require two different Toons' Mastery quests to be purchased, the first being [[Blot]], and the second being Yatta (requiring Poppy's masteries to acquire Looey).
*Waxwell's [[Ability]] could play into his nature, with his ignition being him trying to cause trouble and his trail giving {{Debuff|Ignited}} to [[Toons]] being the backfiring of his pranks.
*Waxwell is the second confirmed antagonist of the [[Show]], the first being {{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}}.
*Waxwell is one of two [[Toons]] with a different render for their Character Card Profile "(image)", the other one being [[Shrimpo]].
*Waxwell and {{CI|Dyle|name=true}} seem to be the only [[Toons]] whose teeth can seemingly change from being flat and sharp. Waxwell has flat teeth in his model and render, but he can be seen with sharp teeth in his [[Sticker]] and a part in the Queens of Mischief music video where he tries to make the power go out.
